  "_comment": "Harborline Transit Authority: the pre-CDE capstone WINDOWS hardening box (single DC for harborline.local; os contains 'win' so nakon uses its powershell deploy path -- SSH transport, Windows OpenSSH, run.ps1 with per-step scripts; elevation comes from the SSH principal, which must be a domain admin here). It consolidates the whole Windows vulnerability universe from pinecrest-hospital (local-host hardening: accounts, password policy, registry, SMB/shares/ACLs/hosts, services, run-key/task/service persistence) and meridian-hq (AD: users, groups, delegation, AS-REP/DES, DCSync ACL, GPP, GPO persistence, LDAP signing, firewall) and adds new categories: Defender neutering + PowerShell logging off, WDigest cleartext + LSA PPL off + NTLM downgrade + anonymous enumeration (legacy credential/protocol exposure), IFEO debugger hijacks, Winlogon Userinit extension, WMI event-subscription persistence, a startup-folder item, AlwaysInstallElevated, and a PasswordNotRequired domain account. Every ad-*/gpp-*/gpo-*/ldap-*/firewall-allow/-win configuration is a GENERIC var-driven seed in boxbuilder/vulndb_vuln_configs/. ORDER MATTERS: weak-password-policy-win runs FIRST (weak domain policy + complexity off before weak account passwords are set); users are created before group-adds and before the DCSync ACL (its trustee must exist); insecure-file-acl-win runs BEFORE insecure-smb-share-win (the share target dir exists); hosts-redirect-win LAST (mirrors pinecrest). Name discipline: every USERNAME / GROUP / ACCOUNT / SPN / RUN_VALUE_NAME / TASK_NAME / SERVICE_NAME / PAYLOAD_PATH / RULE_NAME / GPO_NAME / SHARE_NAME / FILE_PATH / IP / PASSWORD here MUST match its paired check's collect params in scenario.yaml byte-identically -- nothing cross-validates. Password-vs-display-name trap: New-ADUser creates the account DISABLED when the password violates complexity against the display name/description tokens (meridian gotcha) -- every planted password below was chosen to clear that check. The two malicious services are real running services (SCM wrapper exe launching powershell.exe -File <payload>, sc failure auto-restart), scored by process_state on the payload filename fragment (fleetsync / regboost) plus service_state active/enabled -- rename a PAYLOAD_PATH and you must update the matching collect.pattern in scenario.yaml. Guest/audit/smb1/firewall/ldap-signing/spooler/uac/nla are scored; Guest is planted by guest-enabled-win (verify it flips the DOMAIN Guest on a DC -- hardening uses Set-ADUser Guest -Enabled $false); Spooler is scored but NOT planted (running+auto is the Server default -- that insecure default is the finding); LLMNR, audit Process Creation/User Account Management are likewise scored-but-not-planted default-state findings. The roasting rotation target svc_sched must exist AND stay enabled (hardening = rotate the password); rogue accounts score DISABLED-not-deleted.",
